# Anti-Patterns to Avoid

## React Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Excessive Props Drilling

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Passing props through multiple levels
<App user={user}>
  <Layout user={user}>
    <Sidebar user={user}>
      <UserMenu user={user} />

// ✅ GOOD: Use Context or global state
const { user } = useAuth();
```

### ❌ useEffect for Everything

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Deriving state in useEffect
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState('');
useEffect(() => {
  setFullName(`${firstName} ${lastName}`);
}, [firstName, lastName]);

// ✅ GOOD: Calculate directly
const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`;
```

### ❌ State That Should Be Derived

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Duplicated state
const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
const [itemCount, setItemCount] = useState(0);

// ✅ GOOD: Derive it
const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
const itemCount = items.length;
```

### ❌ Mutating State Directly

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Direct mutation
items.push(newItem);
setItems(items);

// ✅ GOOD: Create new array
setItems([...items, newItem]);
```

## TypeScript Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Unnecessary Type Assertions

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const user = data as User;

// ✅ GOOD: Type guard
function isUser(data: unknown): data is User {
  return typeof data === 'object' && data !== null && 'id' in data;
}
```

### ❌ Ignoring TypeScript Errors

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
// @ts-ignore
// @ts-expect-error
const x: any = ...

// ✅ GOOD: Type correctly or use unknown
```

## Architecture Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Business Logic in Components

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Component with complex logic
function BookingPage() {
  const validateSlot = () => { /* 50 lines */ };
  const calculatePrice = () => { /* 30 lines */ };
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD: Extract to hooks/services
function BookingPage() {
  const { validateSlot, calculatePrice } = useBookingLogic();
}
```

### ❌ Giant Components

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: 500+ line component
// ✅ GOOD: Split into small components < 150 lines
```

### ❌ Circular Imports

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: A imports B, B imports A
// ✅ GOOD: Extract common dependency to shared module
```

## Performance Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Creating Functions in Render

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: New function on every render
<Button onClick={() => handleClick(id)}>

// ✅ GOOD: useCallback if necessary
const handleItemClick = useCallback(() => handleClick(id), [id]);
```

### ❌ Inline Objects/Arrays in Props

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: New object on every render
<Component style={{ margin: 10 }} />

// ✅ GOOD: Constant or useMemo
const style = useMemo(() => ({ margin: 10 }), []);
```
